    "finalText": "Done. The implementation is complete and verified:\n\n- **`server.js`** — Express 5 API with all endpoints (`POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/:code`, `GET /r/:code`), knex + `pg` persistence, atomic click increments, and 409/422/404 JSON error handling\n- **`migrations/001_create_links.js`** + **`migrate.js`** — tracked migrations run by `start.sh` before serving on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground\n- **`knexfile.js`** — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment, no hard-coded credentials\n- **`README.md`** — startup instructions (`sh start.sh`)\n\nI tested every requirement via HTTP: status codes and body shapes, code length boundaries (4/20/21), URL returned unchanged, malformed JSON → 422, duplicate codes → 409, redirect Location exact-match, exactly +10 clicks under 10 concurrent redirects, list ordering, and data surviving a restart. The database is left empty with the schema migrated, and port 8000 is free for the test harness."
